marvel readers have been familiar with  venom for decades but the half alien  anti-hero is only just now making his  standalone big screen debut from who's  playing who to the comics you need to  brush up on  here's everything you need to know  before you see venom  a symbiote story also known as the  klyntars the symbiotes are a race of  extraterrestrial fully sentient  parasites  they live by cocooning living organisms  and feeding off their adrenaline  sucking hosts dry before leaving them  for dead the venom symbiote is unique in  its  species for desiring long-lasting bonds  over quick kills  a trait which makes it an outcast making  its first appearance in a string of 1984  comics  the venom symbiote originally attached  itself to peter parker  in the form of a black spider-man suit  while peter initially enjoyed the  benefits of the symbiote he worked to  rid himself of it after he discovered  its villainous nature  eventually driving it away by exploiting  its weakness to loud sounds  a new host the best known human half of  venom is eddie brock  played by tom hardy in the 2018 film  created by david michelani and todd  mcfarland  the character made its first  full-fledged appearance in a 1988 issue  of amazing spider-man  in the comics brock is a once respected  reporter who lost his job as an indirect  result of spider-man's crime fighting  specifically he's fired after a  high-profile story about a serial  killer's true identity is discredited  after spider-man nabs the real culprit  furious in seeking guidance  the catholic brock takes refuge in a  church the same church whose loud bells  peter successfully used to separate from  the symbiote after they encounter each  other brock and the symbiote bond over a  shared hatred of spider-man  and venom as we know him is born  existing outside of the marvel cinematic  universe the venom movie  significantly tweaks brock's original  story removing the peter parker element  and setting the action entirely in  brock's home city of san francisco  in the movie venom bonds with brock  without ever encountering peter parker  as you can tell from the lack of white  spider markings on the movie venom suit  adapting the source while the venom  movie is an original story  it's based on two distinct marvel comic  arcs the first  1993's lethal protector is a six-issue  story that sees spider-man and venom  arranging a truce with the latter  agreeing to leave new york for san  francisco  venom takes up a role as a bay area  anti-hero eventually teaming up with  spider-man again to fend off five new  villainous symbiotes  the second chunk of source material is  1995's planet of the symbiotes a  five-issue arc which also follows venom  and his allies  as they work to stop a worldwide  symbiote invasion combine the two  together and you get the movie's story  of a brutal west coast superhero  protecting san francisco from his  violent fellow aliens  the life foundation in the comics the  shady organization of survivalists  called the life foundation  was formed during the cold war by people  who believed that the world was headed  for a nuclear holocaust  to ensure the survival of civilized life  on earth the foundation built a massive  fallout shelter for survivors  or at least those wealthy enough to buy  themselves a space  to protect the shelter in its  inhabitants the life foundation  kidnapped venom and used them to create  five new symbiotes agony phage lasher  scream and riot all of which get bonded  to life foundation employees  reportedly the big bad and venom will be  the formidable riot  latching himself primarily under riz  ahmed's character life foundation boss  carlton drake dreams of carnage  venom's most famous symbiote nemesis is  carnage an  unhinged offshoot of venom that latches  onto the psychotic killer cletus cassidy  though sony has tried to keep his  involvement a secret  cassidy is reportedly being played in  the film by woody harrelson  though that doesn't necessarily mean  that carnage himself is showing up  speaking to collider harrelson said his  appearance in venom is more of a setup  for the future while the actor did not  confirm he was playing cassidy  he hinted at the sequel tease nature of  his role saying i'm in a little fraction  of this movie but i'll be in the next  one you know  she venom michelle williams stars in  venom is anne wayne who in the comics is  a hot shot lawyer and eddie brock's  ex-wife  the movie makes tweaks to their  relationship making her brock's current  girlfriend as opposed to his ex  much like cletus cassidy anne is another  character with some secret significance  in the comics wayne becomes the  character she venom gaining the powers  of the symbiote after brock allows the  two to bond  williams has already made it clear that  the movie anne will be no pushover but  will she really transform into she venom  probably not in this one more likely  she's in the movie as a seed of what  could come  if venom does well enough to warrant its  own sequels you can bet we'll see more  famous symbiotes taking turns in the  spotlight
 

